socrates: the ABL-handoff dance — fDeviceInit, bBootLUNEn, SSU POWER_CONDITION=ACTIVE

The ABL's handoff (Plan B: the shim does not wake the device) leaves the
link UP but the device refusing SCSI. The chain, each step proven by a
flash photo + the M2 rounds:

- TUR retries -> CHECK CONDITION (flash #7).
- fDeviceInit: SET + flag poll (flash #8/#9 - the flag reads clear, the
  ABL already ran bring-up; the SET itself draws 0xFF, read the flag
  anyway: the shim v19 logic).
- Still key 2 / ASC-ASCQ 04-02 'INITIALIZING COMMAND REQUIRED'
  (flash #10, user-read sense).
- bBootLUNEn: the ABL disables the boot LU (v16: bBootLUNEn=0); the
  shim's green recipe re-enables it (WRITE_ATTR idn 0x00 = 1) BEFORE any
  SSU - flash #11's SSU drew INVALID FIELD without this gate.
- SSU POWER_CONDITION = ACTIVE (byte 4 = 0x11; the plain START_VALID
  form draws 05/24 - the shim's v17/v18).
- Final TUR retries, then the GPT lookup.

The chain lives in its own blocks between the first TUR loop and the
partition lookup; the 00xx patches own that function's interior, so this
rides after the series (0028's context is patched by 0030/0034
byte-for-byte).
---
bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
1 file changed, 46 insertions(+)

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -929,6 +929,37 @@
 		for (int i = 0; i < 3 && (error = ufs_scsi(tur, sizeof(tur), 0, false)); i++) {
 		}
 	}
+	if (error) {
+		/* socrates flash #7 (Plan B): the ABL's handoff leaves the link UP but
+		 * the device in needs-init state - TUR CHECK-CONDITIONs on every retry. */
+		error = ufs_dev_init();
+		if (!error) {
+			static const uint8_t tur2[6] = { 0x00 };
+			for (int i = 0; i < 3 && (error = ufs_scsi(tur2, sizeof(tur2), 0, false)); i++) {
+			}
+		}
+	}
+	if (error) {
+		/* socrates flash #11 (2026-11-07): TUR still refuses with sense key 2 /
+		 * ASC-ASCQ 04-02 'INITIALIZING COMMAND REQUIRED' after the flag poll.
+		 * The M2 green recipe has TWO more steps before SSU: the ABL disables
+		 * the boot LU (bBootLUNEn=0, the v16 panel), and the shim re-enables it
+		 * (WRITE_ATTR idn 0x00 = 1) - the SSU drew INVALID FIELD until then. */
+		int aerr = ufs_query_val(0x04, 0x00, 0x81, 1u << 16);  /* WRITE_ATTR bBootLUNEn=1 */
+		printf("SWEET UFS: bBootLUNEn rc %d\n", aerr);
+		if (!aerr) {
+			/* START STOP UNIT with POWER_CONDITION = ACTIVE (byte 4 = 0x11;
+			 * the plain START_VALID form draws 05/24 - the shim's v17/v18). */
+			static const uint8_t ssu[6] = { 0x1b, 0, 0, 0, 0x11, 0 };
+			error = ufs_scsi(ssu, sizeof(ssu), 0, false);
+			printf("SWEET UFS: SSU ACTIVE rc %d\n", error);
+			if (!error) {
+				static const uint8_t tur3[6] = { 0x00 };
+				for (int i = 0; i < 3 && (error = ufs_scsi(tur3, sizeof(tur3), 0, false)); i++) {
+				}
+			}
+		}
+	}
 	if (!error) {
 		error = ufs_find_partition(want);
 	}
